# Spendo server configuration.
#
# Put your Postgres connection string here. Nothing else is required to run.
#
#   DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host:5432/spendo
#
# This file is read by server/src/index.js at boot and is listed in .gitignore.
# Never commit it: the connection string is a credential.

DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host:5432/spendo

# Port the server listens on. It serves both the API and the app itself.
PORT=8123

# TLS to Postgres. Leave unset and it is worked out from the host: off for
# localhost, on (without certificate verification) for anything else, which is what
# every hosted provider needs.
#
#   disable    no TLS
#   no-verify  TLS, do not verify the certificate  (Supabase, Neon, Railway, Render)
#   verify     TLS, verify the certificate         (your own CA)
#
# PGSSL=no-verify

# --- Sign-in email --------------------------------------------------------
#
# Brevo's HTTP API sends the six-digit sign-in code. The sender address must be
# verified on the Brevo account or every send is refused; the display name is
# free text and is not verified.
#
# Leave BREVO_API_KEY empty and the code is printed to the server console
# instead of emailed. That is enough to test signing in end to end, and enough
# to run the app for one person.
BREVO_API_KEY=
MAIL_FROM_EMAIL=
MAIL_FROM_NAME=Spendo

# --- The model -------------------------------------------------------------
#
# NVIDIA NIM, which speaks the OpenAI chat-completions shape. Used for two
# things only: guessing a category from a description the phone could not
# place, and writing up a month from figures the phone computed.
#
# Leave NIM_API_KEY empty and both fall back cleanly - the category guess uses
# the phone's own history and a keyword table, and a month review shows its
# figures without the written summary. Nothing breaks.
NIM_API_KEY=
# NIM_MODEL=meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct
# NIM_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1/chat/completions
# NIM_TIMEOUT_MS=8000
# AI_CALLS_PER_HOUR=200
